<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abul Hasan Qutb Shah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1699">1699</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Tana Shah, Abul Hasan Tana Shah</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abul Hasan Qutb Shah, known as Tana Shah, was the last sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golconda-fort">Golconda</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a>, reigning from 1672 to 1687. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmins">Brahmin</a> ministers Madanna and Akkanna ran the government. The Mughal emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aurangzeb">Aurangzeb</a> besieged Golconda for eight months and took it by treachery in 1687, imprisoning him at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daulatabad">Daulatabad</a>, where he died in 1699.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abul-hasan-qutb-shah.jpg" alt="Abul Hasan Qutb Shah" width="300" height="417" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: thesandiegomuseumofartcollection · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Sultan_Abu%27l_Hasan_of_Golconda,_Standing_(6124509941).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
